{"title":"Two-dimensional wave equation","markdown":{"headingText":"Two-dimensional wave equation","headingAttr":{"id":"sec-wave2d","classes":[],"keyvalue":[]},"containsRefs":false,"markdown":"\n`apps/wave2d` — the reference for **coupled first-order systems** and for\nmixed boundary conditions.\n\n## Physical setting\n\nAcoustic propagation on a two-dimensional slab. The application is the\nsmallest shipped example of two prognostic fields advanced together, and of a\ndomain that is periodic in one direction and physically bounded in the other.\n\n## Governing equations\n\nThe second-order wave equation $u_{tt} = c^2\\nabla^2 u$ is written as a\ncoupled first-order system in displacement and velocity:\n\n$$\n\\partial_t u \\;=\\; v,\n\\qquad\n\\partial_t v \\;=\\; c^2\\,\\nabla^2 u ,\n$$ {#eq-w2-pde}\n\nwith $\\nabla^2 = \\partial_{xx} + \\partial_{yy}$ on an $n_z = 1$ slab.\n\nWriting it this way is what lets a single stepper advance a tuple of\nincrements $(\\mathrm{d}u, \\mathrm{d}v)$, which is the pattern any multi-field\napplication reuses.\n\n## Boundary conditions\n\nPeriodic in $x$, handled by MPI halo exchange. In $y$ the slab is physically\nbounded, with homogeneous **Dirichlet** ($u = 0$) or **Neumann**\n($\\partial_y u = 0$) conditions applied as a ghost-cell correction after the\nperiodic exchange.\n\nThe ordering matters: the exchange is unconditional and the physical\ncorrection overwrites the ghost values it produced on the boundary faces. This\nkeeps the mixed case from needing a separate communication pattern.\n\n## Finite-difference formulation\n\nCentred stencils, either a fixed second-order Laplacian\n(`wave2d_fd_manual`) or even orders 2–20 (`wave2d_fd`). The Laplacian\ncomponents are accumulated as *unscaled* stencil sums and multiplied by\n$1/\\Delta x^2$, $1/\\Delta y^2$ in the model's right-hand side, which keeps the\nstencil evaluator independent of the grid metric.\n\nTime stepping is explicit, with the hyperbolic CFL condition\n\n$$\n\\Delta t \\;\\lesssim\\; \\frac{1}{c}\\left(\\frac{1}{\\Delta x^2}\n                                     + \\frac{1}{\\Delta y^2}\\right)^{-1/2}.\n$$ {#eq-w2-cfl}\n\nNote this is $\\Delta t \\sim \\Delta x$, not the $\\Delta x^2$ of a parabolic\nproblem: a wave equation is far less stiff than a diffusion equation at the\nsame resolution, and much less stiff than the high-order operators in the\nspectral chapters.\n\n## Verification\n\n* **Runge–Kutta convergence.** Observed temporal order matches the scheme.\n* **Operator evaluation.** The Laplacian evaluator is checked against known\n  inputs.\n* **RHS structure.** Structural tests on the right-hand side pattern.\n* **CPU–GPU parity.** Where GPU twins are built.\n\n## Binaries and inputs\n\n`wave2d_fd_manual`, `wave2d_fd`, plus `wave2d_cuda` / `wave2d_hip` when\nenabled. Command-line driven, with optional VTK output (`--vtk`,\n`--vtk-every`).\n\n## Scalability\n\nNot measured.\n","srcMarkdownNoYaml":""},"formats":{"html":{"identifier":{"display-name":"HTML","target-format":"html","base-format":"html"},"execute":{"fig-width":7,"fig-height":5,"fig-format":"retina","fig-dpi":96,"df-print":"default","error":false,"eval":true,"cache":null,"freeze":false,"echo":true,"output":true,"warning":true,"include":true,"keep-md":false,"keep-ipynb":false,"ipynb":null,"enabled":null,"daemon":null,"daemon-restart":false,"debug":false,"ipynb-filters":[],"ipynb-shell-interactivity":null,"plotly-connected":true,"engine":"markdown"},"render":{"keep-tex":false,"keep-typ":false,"keep-source":false,"keep-hidden":false,"prefer-html":false,"output-divs":true,"output-ext":"html","fig-align":"default","fig-pos":null,"fig-env":null,"code-fold":"none","code-overflow":"scroll","code-link":false,"code-line-numbers":false,"code-tools":false,"tbl-colwidths":"auto","merge-includes":true,"inline-includes":false,"preserve-yaml":false,"latex-auto-mk":true,"latex-auto-install":true,"latex-clean":true,"latex-min-runs":1,"latex-max-runs":10,"latex-makeindex"